      },
      "message": "fix(import): tessellate three-fillet corner blends instead of refusing them\n\nThe corner blend where three rounds meet is a rational patch with one side\ncollapsed to the corner vertex. Two faults kept a rounded-edge STEP from\nimporting:\n\n- At the pole truck's parameter search returns the free parameter anywhere\n  (-1.2e9 on the #1536 model, knot domain 0..1). truck then subdivides the\n  bounding box of the boundary's parameters, a billion knot spans of\n  extrapolation, which never converges: the #1536 hang, #1546's refusal.\n  step_pole brings such an answer back inside the knot domain when the\n  surface there is the same point.\n- The rounded edges are SURFACE_CURVEs whose master is a pcurve. truck\n  rebuilds them in its own parametrisation of the neighbouring surface, and\n  every planar face lost a corner: the model imported at 13,981 mm3 of\n  19,549.7 with no refusal. step_edge3d reads such an edge from its 3D\n  curve directly (switching only the master makes truck invert a\n  same_sense = .F. edge twice).\n\nThe #1536 model, rebuilt with solidcore (62 faces, 126 edges, 66 vertices),\nnow imports closed at 19,545.21 mm3 against the stated 19,549.71.\n\nPinned by import_step_corner_blend on testdata/models/fillet_corner.step\n(one corner of that part) and by step_pole's unit tests.\n\nBuilds on #1546 (merged): its meter still bounds every face.\n\nFixes #1548\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
